# Project Conventions

## Stack

- TypeScript 6.0, React 19, Next.js 16.2 (App Router)
- SCSS Modules for styling, clsx for class composition
- next-intl for i18n (messages in `messages/{en,fr,es}.json`)
- lucide-react 1.x for icons (via `components/Icon`)
- Contentful as CMS (data fetched in server components)
- amazon-cognito-identity-js for auth
- Tailwind CSS 4.2 (integrated alongside SCSS Modules)
- Stripe 9.x / react-stripe-js 6.x for payments

## Architecture

- **Server Components** for data fetching (`app/[lang]/` pages, layout)
- **Client Components** marked with `"use client"` for interactivity
- Component files: `components/ComponentName/ComponentName.tsx` + `.module.scss`
- Utils in `utils/` — pure functions, no React imports
- Hooks in `hooks/` — client-side only

### Dashboard Pages (admin/owner/renter)

Dashboard pages use a **server → client split** with cookie-based auth:

- **Thin wrappers** (no data): Server component resolves `params` with `await`, renders client child components directly. No `"use client"` needed.
- **Data pages**: Server component fetches initial data via `fetchWithAuthServerJson()` (reads `idToken` cookie), passes as `initialData` prop to a `*Content.tsx` client component.
- **Interactive pages** (forms, editors, real-time): Stay fully client-side with `"use client"`.

Pattern for data pages:
- `page.tsx` — async server component, fetches data in try/catch (returns `undefined` on failure)
- `*Content.tsx` — `"use client"` component next to page, receives `lang` + `initialData` props
- Hooks accept optional `initialData` to skip initial fetch when server data is available

Server-side auth fetch: `fetchWithAuthServerJson()` from `utils/fetchWithAuthServer.ts`
Use `get*ApiUrl()` helpers for direct backend URLs (not `/api/*` proxy).

## Agent memory

Long-lived stack notes, architecture guardrails, and session learnings: **`.cursor/memory.md`** at the monorepo root. Prefer updating that file over scattering one-off rules.

## Code Style

- Never use `!important` in CSS
- Never add comments that just narrate what code does
- Use `clsx` (imported as `cx` or `clsx`) for conditional class names
- Translations: use `useTranslations()` from next-intl, keys in `messages/*.json`
- All three locale files (en, fr, es) must stay in sync when adding translations
- Prefer editing existing files over creating new ones

## Contentful Data

- Menu data: `extractMenuColumns()` from `utils/menuHelpers.ts`
- Links: `contentfulItemToLink()` from `utils/linkHelpers.ts`
- Pages: `getPageBySlug()` from `utils/content.ts`
- Locales: `getContentfulLocale()` maps app locale to Contentful locale
- Auth-gated links: Contentful Link model has `requiresAuth` boolean — when `true`, the link is hidden from unauthenticated users (filtered in `NavigationInner.tsx`)
- Custom submenus: Contentful Link model has `submenuId` field — maps to code-defined submenus in `components/Navigation/submenuRegistry.ts`

## Contentful Caching (`utils/content.ts`)

- The Contentful SDK uses Axios (not `fetch`), so Next.js fetch cache does not apply — we use `unstable_cache` from `next/cache` to wrap SDK calls
- All cached functions are tagged `"contentful"` for bulk on-demand purge
- Preview mode (`draftMode`) always **skips the cache** — call the raw `fetch*` function directly
- Pattern for adding a new cached Contentful function:
  1. Write the uncached fetcher (`async function fetchThing(…)`)
  2. In the public export, check `preview` — if true call uncached, otherwise wrap in `unstable_cache` with key array, `revalidate`, and `tags: ["contentful"]`
- Use `REVALIDATE_MINUTES` (60s) for page content, `REVALIDATE_HOURS` (3600s) for layout/config
- On-demand revalidation: `POST /api/revalidate` with `x-revalidate-secret` header calls `revalidateTag("contentful")`
- See `docs/ssr-architecture.md` for the full cache profile table and Contentful webhook setup

## Component Patterns

- Icons: `<Icon name="IconName" size={24} />` — name is PascalCase or kebab-case
- Buttons: `<Button variant="primary" size="sm" />` — variants: primary, secondary, toggle, danger, warning, link, ghost
- Sections: wrap in `<SectionConnector>` with section props from Contentful
- Headings: `<Heading as="h1" size="h1">` — `as` is semantic, `size` is visual

